 # Notifications: server part
 
-1. `schema.sql` → run in Supabase.
-2. `notifications.js` → copy to `routes/`, mount it: `app.use('/api/notifications', require('./routes/notifications')(supabase));`
-3. `npm i firebase-admin`; on Render add env var `FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT` (the whole service-account JSON).
-4. Let the server notify by itself for things that already pass through it. In each route, after saving, call
-   `pushToPartner(supabase, { coupleId, fromRole, type, title, body, data })`:
+**Nothing is required.** The server (us-app `routes/auth.js`) already sends every push (chat, calls, hug, touch,
+miss you, partner requests, safety alerts, events, music …) as FCM *data* messages, and already has
+`POST /api/auth/register-fcm-token`. The Android app now uses exactly those.
 
-| Existing route | After it saves, send | Extra `data` |
-|---|---|---|
-| `POST /api/chat` (new message) | `chat_message` — body = the text (or "📷 Photo", "🎤 Voice message") | `fromName` |
-| `POST /api/chat/:id/react` | `chat_reaction` | `fromName` |
-| `POST /api/call/notify` | `call_incoming` | `video: "true"` for video, `fromName` |
-| `POST /api/call/log` with status `missed` | `call_missed` | `fromName` |
-| partner request / accept / unpair routes | `partner_request` / `partner_accepted` / `partner_removed` | `fromName` |
-| location alerts (arrive / leave / SOS) | `location_arrived` / `location_left` / `location_sos` | `fromName`, body = place |
-| `POST /api/pro/...` verified | `pro_update` (send to both roles) | — |
+Only needs on Render: env var `FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT` (already set if the web-app APK gets pushes).
 
-The app itself already asks the server to send: hug / touch / miss you (Home). Any other feature can do the same in one line:
-`notificationSender.toPartner(NotificationType.SURPRISE_NEW)` (Kotlin, `core/notifications/NotificationSender.kt`).
+## Optional: forget this phone on log out
+Without it, a signed-out phone keeps getting the old person's pushes until that person signs in elsewhere.
+Add to `routes/auth.js`, next to `/register-fcm-token`:
 
-Date-based ones (`anniversary`, `memory_throwback`, `milestone`, `*_reminder`) are best sent by a small daily cron on the server
-to both roles; calendar and study reminders are also scheduled on the phone (alarms), so those work with no server.
+```js
+router.post('/unregister-fcm-token', async (req, res) => {
+  const { userId, token } = req.body;
+  if (!userId || !token) return res.status(400).json({ error: 'Missing fields' });
+  await supabase.from('fcm_tokens').delete().eq('user_id', userId).eq('token', token);
+  res.json({ ok: true });
+});
+```
